sections.content:
A **struct** (structure) is a custom data type that groups related data together.

Instead of separate variables:
```bpl
local personName: string = "Alice";
local personAge: int = 30;
local personHeight: float = 1.65;
```

Use a struct:
```bpl
local person: Person = Person { name: "Alice", age: 30, height: 1.65 };
```

Structs help you organize related data into a single, meaningful unit.

languages.BPL:
struct Person {
    name: string,
    age: int,
}

languages.C:
struct Person {
    char* name;
    int age;
};

languages.Rust:
struct Person {
    name: String,
    age: i32,
}

languages.TypeScript:
interface Person {
    name: string;
    age: number;
}

